<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hugh III, Duke of Burgundy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1142–<a href="/years/1192">1192</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capetian-house-of-burgundy">Capetian House of Burgundy</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hugh III was duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> from 1162 to 1192. He took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a> and, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-france">Philip II of France</a> returned home in 1191, commanded the French contingent alongside Richard the Lionheart, fighting at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsuf">Arsuf</a>. He died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a> in 1192. At home he founded the Sainte-Chapelle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dijon">Dijon</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hugh-iii-duke-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="Hugh III, Duke of Burgundy" width="198" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Urbain Plancher, Zacharie Merle - 1739 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hugh_III.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Hugh III</b> commanded the French contingent of the Third Crusade after Philip II returned home in 1191 and died at Acre in 1192, Odo III fought for Philip II at the Battle of Bouvines in 1214, and Hugh IV joined the crusade of Louis IX to Egypt in…</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Duchy of Burgundy · Military</a></li></ul></section>
